From f4520977fda3f2d296034bac882647fae24e5e2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:18:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] fix(view): keep a deforming window with its workspace

The release deferral parks a still-displaced sheet under the shared drag
tree, which lives outside every workspace layer. A workspace switch never
ended that wait: the outgoing workspace re-enabled and re-presented the
view, but its slide offset and clip only reach its own trees, so the
window hung at its old screen position until the spring settled and the
deferred re-home finally dropped it out of sight.

Landing the resting re-home as soon as the view leaves its workspace's
presentation ends the wait: the window is a workspace child again, so it
travels and hides with the workspace and comes back with it. The deferral
still covers the reparents a release issues, including a transfer's park
and re-home onto the active destination.

A window still held by the cursor keeps its drag presentation instead.
The drag tree owns its visibility, so a workspace no longer hides it at
the end of the slide it was carried out of (it used to vanish mid-drag)
and no longer reveals it as its own.

Pinned by drag/settle_workspace_switch: a released sheet is carried out
with a 300 ms slide while a slow spring still deforms it, is absent once
the slide ends, returns with the workspace, and a held window stays drawn
across the switch before landing on the workspace it is dropped on. Both
halves are falsified separately: without the flush the sheet keeps drawing
at its old x mid-slide, without the ownership guard the held window
vanishes at the slide's end.

Validated: meson units 150/150; harness drag/ workspace/ animation/
overview/ transient/ render/title_bar 126 pass, the 2 failures
(animation/drag_toggle, drag/overview_card_workspace_edge_scroll) fail
identically on the parent commit and predate this change; clang-format and
clang-tidy clean.

