From 6b606dadeef4622329105c4bac5f0b5ef9729054 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:52:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] fix(workspace): land the drag-release wait before the
 trees travel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A gesture switches workspace without deactivating the outgoing one until
it commits: slideBegin moves the base workspace's tree under the fingers
and setActive(false) only runs at the release. The first commit's flush
hung off that deactivation, so for the whole swipe a released, still
deforming sheet stayed parked under the shared drag tree — outside the
trees that travel — and snapped into place at commit.

slideBegin now lands every participant's deferred re-home while the trees
are still at rest. The activate path keeps its own flush (deactivation
happens inside the switch), so a swipe and a switch end up in the same
place by different routes.

The pin gains the gesture phase, an explicit linear slide curve (the
default curve is a spring and ignores duration_ms, which made the
"halfway" sample meaningless), and an engagement floor: the sheet must
still move on ordered ticks after the release, otherwise the deferral
under test was never taken and the check would pass vacuously. Its travel
assertion is axis-agnostic and requires the sheet to stay drawn, so
hiding the view on deactivation cannot pass as travelling.

Falsified per mechanism: without the deactivation flush the activate
phase stops travelling; without the slideBegin flush the gesture phase
stops travelling; without the ownership guard the held window vanishes at
the slide's end.

Validated: meson units 150/150; harness drag/ workspace/ animation/
effect/workspace output/ transient/ overview/ 148 pass, the 4 failures
(animation/drag_toggle, drag/overview_card_workspace_edge_scroll,
output/two_output_containment pre-existing on 01540344;
drag/toplevel_drag_lifecycle a load flake that passes in isolation);
clang-format and clang-tidy clean.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit f86099e400f861b037b16301075a4b5fa40c315b)
