From fc31d8f5c9aa13a0c229312e7804a909738ed833 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:19:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] fix(view): let a dragged window's dialogs ride its
 presentation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

External-review round on the workspace-stick delta (M1, M2, L1, N1).

M1: dragPresentationOwnsVisibility() only asked whether the cursor held
this exact view. A dragged window carries its transient children into the
shared drag tree (syncTransientSceneParent), so a workspace deactivation
still disabled an unattached dialog and flushed its wait, and the dialog
vanished mid-drag. The predicate now walks the transient-parent chain: an
ancestor under the cursor owns the presentation of everything riding it.

M2: the same guard protected the view's scene node but left its decoration
shadow written unconditionally, so a held window lost its shadow the
moment its workspace deactivated. Both writes now sit behind the guard.
Not pinned: the harness draws no window shadow in this configuration (a
band under a resting window measures the bare backdrop), so there is
nothing to measure; the fix mirrors the node guard.

L1: the pin exercised only a cancelled swipe. It now drives a committed
swipe as well — the window travels with the slide, the release lands on
the next workspace, and the window leaves the screen with its workspace —
and asserts the cancelled swipe returns it to rest on its own workspace.

N1: the clipped-at-the-edge case in assert_travelled now also requires the
drawn sheet to be smaller than its own box, so a window that merely sat on
the edge cannot pass as having travelled.

M1 is falsified: with the single-view predicate restored, the new phase
fails at "the drag's child dialog was hidden with the workspace".

Validated: meson units 150/150; harness drag/ workspace/ animation/
transient/ focus/transient 99 pass, the 2 failures
(animation/drag_toggle, drag/overview_card_workspace_edge_scroll)
pre-existing on the base; clang-format and clang-tidy clean.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8c8ee7954177982d3930743409485e84e2d71db8)
---
